red (VTI-EVT-004).","type":"string","enum":["draft","published","cancelled"]},"When":{"title":"When","description":"When the event happens, in JSCalendar\'s terms. `start` is local time in `timeZone`; `duration` is how long it lasts. With `showWithoutTime` true it is an all-day event: `start`\'s time MUST be `T00:00:00` and `duration` whole days (VTI-EVT-005).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["start","timeZone","duration"],"properties":{"start":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/LocalDateTime"},"timeZone":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/TimeZoneId"},"duration":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/JSCalendarDuration"},"showWithoutTime":{"type":"boolean","description":"An all-day event. Absent means false."}}},"JSCalendarDuration":{"title":"JSCalendarDuration","description":"A non-negative duration in the subset of ISO 8601 JSCalendar uses: `P` then weeks or days, then `T` with hours, minutes and seconds, such as `PT1H30M`, `P1D` or `P2W`. No months or years. Used only for `When.duration`, which carries JSCalendar\'s own member and encoding verbatim; this family\'s own offsets are integers naming their unit (`ReminderMinutes`).","type":"string","minLength":3,"maxLength":32,"pattern":"^P(?!\$)([0-9]+W)?([0-9]+D)?(T(?=[0-9])([0-9]+H)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+S)?)?\$"},"TimeZoneId":{"title":"TimeZoneId","description":"An IANA time zone name, such as `Europe/London`, or `Etc/UTC`. A responder MUST refuse a name its time zone database does not know.","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":64,"pattern":"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_+-]*(/[A-Za-z0-9_+-]+){0,2}\$"},"LocalDateTime":{"title":"LocalDateTime","description":"A local date and time with no offset, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS`, as JSCalendar\'s LocalDateTime. Read in the event\'s `timeZone`.","type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9]{4}-(0[1-9]|1[0-2])-(0[1-9]|[12][0-9]|3[01])T([01][0-9]|2[0-3]):[0-5][0-9]:[0-5][0-9]\$"},"EventTitle":{"title":"EventTitle","type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":200,"description":"A short name. Plain text; a reader MUST NOT treat it as instructions."},"EventId":{"title":"EventId","description":"Opaque identifier of an event: `evt_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, community-scoped, never reused (VTI-EVT-001).","type":"string","pattern":"^evt_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"Registration":{"title":"Registration","description":"One registrant\'s registration for one event. The registrant reads all of it; a host reads all of it; another registrant on a `visible` roster reads only `entryId`, `status` and `guests` (VTI-EVT-053). Exactly one of `entryId` (a member) and `registrantDid` (a partner\'s member, VTI-EVT-134) names the registrant.","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["registrationId","eventId","status","guests","roster","eventSequence","createdAt","updatedAt"],"properties":{"registrationId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationId"},"eventId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventId"},"entryId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EntryId","description":"The registrant\'s directory entry, where they are a member. Exactly one of `entryId` and `registrantDid` is present."},"registrantDid":{"type":"string","minLength":8,"maxLength":2048,"pattern":"^did:[a-z0-9]+:[A-Za-z0-9._:%-]+\$","description":"A registrant who is not a member of the community — a partner\'s member (VTI-EVT-134) — by the DID they presented as. Shown to the event\'s hosts and to the registrant only."},"status":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationStatus"},"guests":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"maximum":10,"description":"Plus-ones the registrant brings."},"answers":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationAnswers","description":"The registrant\'s and the hosts\' view only."},"codeOfConductAcknowledged":{"type":"string","pattern":"^[0-9a-f]{64}\$","description":"The `sha256` of the code of conduct the registrant acknowledged."},"waitlistPosition":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"While `waitlisted`: the registrant\'s place in the queue, 1 first."},"roster":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RosterSetting","description":"The roster setting the registration was made under (VTI-EVT-052)."},"eventSequence":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"description":"The event\'s `sequence` when the registration last changed, so a registrant sees whether the event changed since."},"note":{"type":"string","minLength":1,"maxLength":500,"description":"A host\'s note on a decline or removal, shown to the registrant. Plain text."},"createdAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"},"updatedAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"}}},"EventInstant":{"title":"EventInstant","type":"string","format":"date-time","description":"An RFC 3339 instant in UTC, whole seconds, such as `2026-11-30T18:30:00Z`."},"RosterSetting":{"title":"RosterSetting","description":"Who may see who is registered (VTI-EVT-050). `visible`: registrants who are going or maybe see each other. `hidden`: no registrant sees another; the event\'s hosts do. Fixed once the event is published (VTI-EVT-051) and recorded on each registration (VTI-EVT-052).","type":"string","enum":["visible","hidden"]},"RegistrationAnswers":{"title":"RegistrationAnswers","description":"Answers keyed by `questionId`.","type":"object","maxProperties":20,"propertyNames":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationQuestionId"},"additionalProperties":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/RegistrationAnswer"}},"RegistrationAnswer":{"title":"RegistrationAnswer","description":"An answer to a question: a string for `text` and `choice`, a boolean for `boolean`.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","maxLength":500},{"type":"boolean"}]},"RegistrationQuestionId":{"title":"RegistrationQuestionId","type":"string","pattern":"^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,31}\$","description":"A question\'s key within its event."},"RegistrationStatus":{"title":"RegistrationStatus","description":"Where a registration stands (VTI-EVT-032). `going`: has a place. `maybe`: has said maybe; holds no place. `pending`: awaits a host\'s decision. `waitlisted`: waits for a place, in order. `withdrawn`: the registrant withdrew. `declined`: a host declined a pending registration. `removed`: a host removed it.","type":"string","enum":["going","maybe","pending","waitlisted","withdrawn","declined","removed"]},"RegistrationId":{"title":"RegistrationId","description":"Opaque identifier of one registrant\'s registration for one event: `reg_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random and unique within the community; a registrant has at most one registration per event (VTI-EVT-030).","type":"string","pattern":"^reg_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"EntryId":{"title":"EntryId","description":"Opaque identifier of one directory entry: `dir_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters. Random, scoped to one community, and stable for the life of the membership — it survives a rotation of the member\'s DID, which is why groups, notes and cards are keyed by it. It MUST NOT be derived from, and MUST NOT reveal, any DID of the member, and the same person\'s entries in two communities MUST NOT share one. Compared by exact string equality.","type":"string","pattern":"^dir_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"},"EventInvitation":{"title":"EventInvitation","description":"One member\'s invitation to one event (VTI-EVT-102). Seen by the event\'s hosts and by the invitee; never by anyone else (VTI-EVT-106).","type":"object","additionalProperties":false,"required":["invitationId","eventId","entryId","invitedBy","replyExpected","answer","createdAt"],"properties":{"invitationId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInvitationId"},"eventId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventId"},"entryId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EntryId","description":"The invitee."},"invitedBy":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInviter"},"inviterEntryId":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EntryId","description":"The host or member who invited, where `invitedBy` is `host` or `member`. Shown to hosts only."},"replyExpected":{"type":"boolean","description":"The event was `expect` when the invitation was made (VTI-EVT-100)."},"answer":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInvitationAnswer"},"answeredAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"},"revoked":{"type":"boolean","description":"A host revoked it (VTI-EVT-103); its notification was withdrawn. Absent means false."},"createdAt":{"\$ref":"#/\$defs/EventInstant"}}},"EventInvitationAnswer":{"title":"EventInvitationAnswer","description":"The invitee\'s answer (VTI-EVT-104). `none`: not answered. `going`, `maybe`: answered by registering. `declined`: the invitee said they will not come — recorded here and nowhere else; not a host\'s decline of a registration.","type":"string","enum":["none","going","maybe","declined"]},"EventInviter":{"title":"EventInviter","description":"Who invited (VTI-EVT-106). `audience`: the community, under the event\'s invitation mode (VTI-EVT-101). `host`: a host, by name (VTI-EVT-103). `member`: a member of the audience (VTI-EVT-105). `link`: the invitee redeemed an invitation link (VTI-EVT-107).","type":"string","enum":["audience","host","member","link"]},"EventInvitationId":{"title":"EventInvitationId","description":"Opaque identifier of one invitation to one event: `inv_` followed by 16 to 64 base64url characters.","type":"string","pattern":"^inv_[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,64}\$"}}}';

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the request variant, taken from this
/// specification's front matter.
///
/// Pass it to [consumeInbound] — items 5b, 7 and 8 are per-specification and
/// cannot be derived from the document alone, and item 2 needs the schema it
/// carries.
const SpecPolicy spec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: typeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: payloadSchemaJson,
);

/// The SPEC §7.2 policy for the success-response variant.
///
/// `isRecipientRequired` tracks the *issuer* party's requirement, because a
/// response swaps the parties (§7.3 item 5).
const SpecPolicy responseSpec = SpecPolicy(
  typeUri: responseTypeUri,
  isBearer: false,
  isProofRequired: true,
  isRecipientRequired: true,
  isIssuedAtRequired: true,
  payloadSchema: responsePayloadSchemaJson,
);
